    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d823">

                <pb facs="0672" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Russian Issue/59: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-18T11:00:00+08:00">February 18, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 18—10:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. Department’s 18, January 30, 3 p.m. concerning Russian issue of
                    reorganization loan. Under my instructions Paxton<anchor n="90" xml:id="d823-f1"
                    /> saw Jabin Hsu, Director of Domestic Affairs of the Ministry of Finance, and
                    with my approval has furnished to him copies of the letters dated June 5, 1936
                    signed by W. E. Hurry and July 15, 1936 signed by Sir Leonard Franklin,<anchor
                        n="91" xml:id="d823-f2"/> showing that British bondholders have received 30
                    percent <pb facs="0673" n="665" xml:id="pg665"/> of face value stating Hsu
                    promised to look into the matter. Further developments will be reported.</p>
                <p>Copy to Peiping by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d823-f1" n="90" xml:id="d823-f1-content">
                <p>J. Hall Paxton, Second Secretary of Embassy in China, at Nanking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d823-f2" n="91" xml:id="d823-f2-content">
                <p>Letters not printed; see Department’s instruction No. 252, September 5, 1936,
                        <ref target="frus1936v04#pg_595"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1936, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>, p.
                        595</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
